%% AI request flow for the first vertical slice (PROPOSED design, not implemented or tested)
%% Flow: onboarding (prior) -> AuthN/AuthZ -> LLM gateway -> inference -> usage and trace reporting
%% Source: docs/02-enterprise-ai-architecture/llm-gateway-model-serving.md sections 2-3
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant App as Tenant Application
  participant Entra as Microsoft Entra ID
  participant GW as LLM Gateway
  participant Cache as Config Cache (signed snapshot)
  participant RL as Rate-Limit Store
  participant BR as Amazon Bedrock
  participant UP as Usage Pipeline
  participant OT as Observability Pipeline

  App->>Entra: Request access token (workload identity)
  Entra-->>App: OIDC access token
  App->>GW: POST inference request + token + trace context
  GW->>Cache: Validate token (cached JWKS) and check revocation list
  alt Token invalid, expired or revoked
    GW-->>App: 401 authentication error + trace ID
  else Token valid
    GW->>Cache: Evaluate policy (tenant, project, role, model entitlement, classification)
    alt Policy denies
      GW-->>App: 403 authorization error + trace ID
    else Policy allows
      GW->>RL: Check and increment rate and token limits
      alt Limit exceeded
        RL-->>GW: Over limit
        GW-->>App: 429 rate or quota error + retry guidance
      else Within limits
        RL-->>GW: OK
        GW->>BR: Invoke resolved model (AWS SDK via PrivateLink)
        alt Provider success
          BR-->>GW: Completion + token counts
          GW-->>App: 200 response + token counts + trace ID
        else Provider error or timeout
          BR-->>GW: Error
          GW-->>App: Failover to approved alternate if configured, else explicit provider error
        end
      end
    end
  end
  GW-)UP: Usage event (tenant, project, principal, model, tokens, status, error class)
  GW-)OT: Spans and metrics (gateway-added latency, upstream latency)
  Note over GW,OT: Usage and telemetry are asynchronous and do not block the response (NFR-005)
